{"name":"Cork","hex":"#5a4c42","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cork","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The principal city of County Cork, Ireland.","A county in the Republic of Ireland (County Cork)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cork"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cork (material)","blocks":[{"text":"Cork is an impermeable buoyant material. It is the phellem layer of bark tissue which is harvested for commercial use primarily from Quercus suber, which is native to southwest Europe and northwest Africa. Cork is composed of suberin, a hydrophobic substance. Because of its impermeable, buoyant, elastic, and fire retardant properties, it is used in a variety of products, the most common of which is wine stoppers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Cork.jpg/330px-Cork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cork_(material)","wikidata":"Q49444"},{"title":"Stopper (plug)","blocks":[{"text":"A stopper, bung, or cork is a cylindrical or conical closure used to seal a container, such as a bottle, tube, or barrel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Jug_with_cork_stopper.jpg/330px-Jug_with_cork_stopper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stopper_(plug)","wikidata":"Q11981837"},{"title":"Cork (city)","blocks":[{"text":"Cork is the second-largest city in the Republic of Ireland, the county town of County Cork, the largest city in the province of Munster and the third-largest on the island of Ireland. At the 2022 census, it had a population of 224,004."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/University_College_Cork_-_Quad_during_Eclipse_2015_%2816684104050%29.jpg/330px-University_College_Cork_-_Quad_during_Eclipse_2015_%2816684104050%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm